WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.960
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:06.480
Fulfillment by Amazon or FBA is a great way

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:10.520
to grow your business and reach more customers.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:14.040
With FBA, Amazon stores your inventory,

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:18.760
ships your orders, and handles returns, and customer service.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:23.280
Your FBA products also become eligible for free shipping

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:26.120
and Amazon Prime 2-day delivery.

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:29.320
This is a great way to maximize exposure and sales

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.480
in the Amazon store.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:36.440
Sellers new to FBA can also enroll in the FBA New Selection

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.160
Program.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.600
The FBA New Selection Program includes free monthly storage,

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:46.260
removals, and return processing for all eligible

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:48.960
new to FBA parent ASINs.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:53.120
Plus, new FBA sellers can receive credits and discounts

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:56.080
for things like advertising and shopping.

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:59.640
Your FBA costs will depend on the products you sell

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:02.400
and the exact services you use.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.640
You may also encounter fees related

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:08.200
to storing and managing your FBA inventory.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.200
There are three tools you can use

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:14.760
to estimate your potential FBA fees in Seller Central.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:17.240
The estimated fee per unit sold column

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:20.200
on the FBA inventory page.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:24.600
The revenue calculator and the fee preview report.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:28.520
To learn more about calculating your potential FBA fees,

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:32.040
you can review our guide, "Is FBA Right for You?"

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.160
in Seller Central.
